kflow para coger los emails que vaya recibiendo y que los clasifiq...", "business_objective": "User requested a new workflow for: crea un workflow para coger los emails que vaya recibiendo y que los clasifique por nivel de urgencia con IA", "desired_outcome": "Deliver an abstract workflow plan that satisfies: crea un workflow para coger los emails que vaya recibiendo y que los clasifique por nivel de urgencia con IA", "workflow_summary": "Abstract workflow plan for receiving emails from Gmail, classifying them by urgency (low, medium, high, critical) using AI, and applying the classification result directly to the original email in Gmail without additional storage or notifications.", "stages": [{"id": "stage_1", "name": "Receive New Emails from Gmail", "purpose": "Capture incoming emails from Gmail as they arrive, ensuring immediate processing for urgency classification.", "stage_kind": "trigger_intake", "business_effect": "None; this stage is purely about intake and handoff to the next stage.", "target_entity": "Newly arrived email in Gmail", "user_visible_goal": "User should see newly arrived emails appear in their Gmail inbox as usual, with no immediate visible change.", "unresolved_decisions": [], "required_capabilities": ["Monitor a Gmail mailbox for new incoming messages in real-time or near-real-time (push-based trigger).", "Preserve the full content and metadata of each email (sender, subject, body, timestamps, etc.)."], "expected_inputs": ["A newly arrived email in Gmail with its original sender, subject, body text, headers, and any attached files or metadata."], "expected_outputs": ["The full email content and metadata passed to the next stage for urgency classification."], "dependencies": [], "success_criteria": ["Every new email received in Gmail is captured exactly once and handed off to the classification stage without loss or duplication.", "No emails are missed due to trigger latency; processing should start within a few seconds of arrival."], "notes