query_text:
  Original workflow request: crea un workflow para coger los emails que vaya recibiendo y que los clasifique por nivel de urgencia con IA
  Workflow objective: User requested a new workflow for: crea un workflow para coger los emails que vaya recibiendo y que los clasifique por nivel de urgencia con IA
  Desired outcome: Deliver an abstract workflow plan that satisfies: crea un workflow para coger los emails que vaya recibiendo y que los clasifique por nivel de urgencia con IA
  Workflow summary: Abstract workflow plan for receiving emails, classifying them by urgency level using AI, and applying visible labels to each email without additional notifications or moving emails from the inbox.
  Current stage id: stage_apply_label
  Current stage name: Apply Urgency Label to Email
  Stage purpose: Silently apply the determined urgency label to the original email in Gmail, ensuring no notifications are generated.
  Stage required capabilities: Update an email's labels in Gmail programmatically and silently., Ensure that only the label is modified; no other metadata or content changes are made.
  Stage expected inputs: A stream of emails from the previous stage, each with a single urgency label (low, medium, high, critical, or review).
  Stage expected outputs: Confirmation that the label has been applied to the original email in Gmail without errors.
  Stage dependencies: stage_classify_urgency
  Previous stage node selections: stage_receive_emails: n8n-nodes-base.gmailTrigger | stage_classify_urgency: n8n-nodes-base.openAi
  Clarifications already provided:
  -
  Retrieval focus hint: Prefer nodes that mutate the source item directly, such as adding labels or tags, moving folders, archiving, or updating source-side state. Reject trigger-only or read-only nodes. Treat workflow compatibility as a hard constraint. Preserve the exact source system, trigger style, processing mode, and final outcome named by the user instead of forcing a near match.
